0.9.0
----------
* Breaking: `revoke()` now clears `curr_async_result_id` and detaches the AsyncResult (returning `NOT_SCHEDULED`) after broadcasting the revoke, so a task stuck in `STARTED` after worker loss can be queued again
* Breaking: `revoke()` now returns the resulting task status instead of `None`
* Admin Revoke and Terminate actions are no longer limited to tasks present in the Redis queue; they are available for any scheduled task
* `terminate()` now clears `curr_async_result_id` for running (STARTED) tasks, so the record is detached after termination
* Flower address is resolved from `CELERY_BOOST_FLOWER` (canonical) or the deprecated `CELERY_FLOW_ADDRESS` alias, defaulting to `/flower`; relative paths are resolved against the current request
* add `django_celery_boost.context_processors.flower` to expose `flower_addr` in every template
* add "Concurrency and locks" documentation page with the worker-loss recovery recipe
* Breaking: drop Django 4.2 and Python 3.11/3.12 support; require Python 3.13+
* add Django 6.0 and 6.1 to the test matrix (Python 3.14)
* make Celery timing tests deterministic and add pytest-rerunfailures as a safety net

